Language for describing machines.

(defmachine <name>)

Defines a machine.  This is a state machine which generates
signals and has two busses of interest, called (THE PCBUS <name>)
and (THE NPCBUS <name>).  The width of these busses depends on
the size of the microcode.  The machine can only dispatch on
sources which can be read onto its PCBUS.

(defbus <name> <vectordef>)

Defines a bus with fields described by <vectordef>.
A bus is just a set of wires that people use to communicate on.
Some things can drive it, and some can read it.






<vectordef> is a list of things which, when concatenated, describe
the vector.  The format is:
	<vectordef> ::= (<fieldspec>*)
	<fieldspec> ::= (<integer> <fielddef>*) | <bitname>
	<fielddef> ::= <name> | <vectordef>
